reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991115/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-160643" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "III only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991115/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f82fa702c211b046081b0fcaee8c5a347d50545af66c632d5e643818e7988a1" "basis" 1023 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991115/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-160643" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and III only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991115/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f82fa702c211b046081b0fcaee8c5a347d50545af66c632d5e643818e7988a1" "basis" 1023 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991115/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-160645" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A triangle $S$ has vertices at $(-3,1),(1,-4),(1,0).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the counterclockwise rotation ${R}_{{90}^{∘}}$ by an angle of ${90}^{∘}$ about the origin?\n\n- $(-1,3)$\n- $(4,1)$\n- $(0,-1)$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991115/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f82fa702c211b046081b0fcaee8c5a347d50545af66c632d5e643818e7988a1" "basis" 1023 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991115/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-160645" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The counterclockwise rotation ${R}_{{90}^{∘}}$ by an angle of ${90}^{∘}$ is given by the matrix\n\n$$\nR=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the image of $S$ under the action of ${R}_{{90}^{∘}},$ we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =[\\begin{aligned}\\,-3 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & \\,\\,\\,-4 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under ${R}_{{90}^{∘}}$ by calculating the matrix product $RX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}RX & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}\\,-3 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & \\,\\,\\,-4 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(-1,-3),(4,1),(0,1).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991115/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f82fa702c211b046081b0fcaee8c5a347d50545af66c632d5e643818e7988a1" "basis" 1023 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991115/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-160645" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991115/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "31c2feb4266eff72b427e01802c275f867994df67b826b638bbbd5094a9a83ca" "basis" 1023 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991115/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-160645" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991115/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f82fa702c211b046081b0fcaee8c5a347d50545af66c632d5e643818e7988a1" "basis" 1023 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991115/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-160