c51e135f.png"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003089/state.json" "file_sha256" "f07b529fcc489010236892ec02a2f855802235483748b56921c87bff17bae15d" "basis" 1083 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003089/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-160644" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A triangle $S$ has vertices at $(2,-3),(3,1),(-4,-1).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the counterclockwise rotation ${R}_{{270}^{∘}}$ by an angle of ${270}^{∘}$ about the origin?\n\n- $(3,2)$\n- $(1,-3)$\n- $(-1,4)$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033087/state.json" "file_sha256" "01ae30657cc075b3bf827e699e81b7553edf9f4a4101aca1cb230f5da63669f8" "basis" 1230 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033087/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-160644" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The counterclockwise rotation ${R}_{{270}^{∘}}$ by an angle of ${270}^{∘}$ is given by the matrix\n\n$$\nR=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the image of $S$ under the action of ${R}_{{270}^{∘}},$ we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & -4 \\\\ -3 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under ${R}_{{270}^{∘}}$ by calculating the matrix product $RX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}RX & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & -4 \\\\ -3 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(-3,-2),(1,-3),(-1,4).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033087/state.json" "file_sha256" "01ae30657cc075b3bf827e699e81b7553edf9f4a4101aca1cb230f5da63669f8" "basis" 1230 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033087/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-160644" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033087/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2d1c67a9430405ef72e259fb94771ab456f6453342f406192d9313ada08eb882" "basis" 1230 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033087/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-160644" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033087/state.json" "file_sha256" "01ae30657cc075b3bf827e699e81b7553edf9f4a4101aca1cb230f5da63669f8" "basis" 1230 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033087/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-160644" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and II only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033087/state.json" "file_sha256" "01ae30657cc075b3bf827e699e81b7553edf9f4a4101aca1cb230f5da63669f8" "basis" 1230 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033087/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-160644" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "I only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/questi